WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:03.470
Do you hallucinate. have visions or
believe you see those who are now dead?

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.890
Yes.

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.590
Detective Sergeant Jackie Stevenson

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.950
was a brave and invaluable
member of the police service.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.230
You witnessed the murder of your
colleague less than three weeks ago.

6
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.680
You can't bring Stevie back.

7
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.790
- What does she know?
- Exactly! [RIVER CHUCKLES]

8
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.590
Exactly.

9
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.870
'Do you see ghosts?

10
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.710
- 'I don't believe in ghosts.
- Then what do you see?'

11
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.300
Manifests.

12
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.110
We're all sad. John -- all broken.

13
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.430
I'm glad it was you by
her side when she died.

14
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.080
River. Detective Sergeant King.

15
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.480
Is that my baby-sitter?

16
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.070
We're trying to link that
car to Stevie's murder.

17
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.470
otherwise you chased an
innocent man to his death.

18
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.590
His girlfriend is expecting a baby.
She's already gone to the press.

19
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.880
Yeah. there he is! There's the murderer!

20
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.220
I didn't do it.

21
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.560
Can't sleep?

22
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.640
Guilt does that to you.

23
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.030
What would I shoot a pig for?

24
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.680
Some of them are my best customers.

25
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.310
Then who did?

26
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.870
Then who did?

27
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.760
MUSIC: I'm In The Mood
For Dancing by The Nolans

28
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.640
♪ Ooh. ooh

29
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.470
♪ Yeah. yeah

30
00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:57.390
♪ I'm in the mood for
dancing. romancing... ♪

31
00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.510
Still smells of Chinese.

32
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.870
Didn't you save a fortune cookie?

33
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.590
♪ I'm in the mood for chancing

34
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.750
♪ I feel like dancing

35
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.870
♪ Ooh. so come on and hold me tight

36
00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.310
♪ Dancing

37
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.470
♪ I'm in the mood. babe

38
00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.990
♪ So let the music play

39
00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.310
♪ Ooh. I'm dancing

40
00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.270
♪ I'm in the groove. babe

41
00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:29.230
♪ So get on up and let your body sway

42
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.910
♪ I'm in the mood for dancing. romancing

43
00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.230
♪ You know. I shan't ever stop tonight

44
00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.590
♪ I'm in the mood for chancing... ♪

45
00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.350
They're burying me tomorrow.

46
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.950
♪ I feel like dancing

47
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.670
♪ Ooh. from head to my toes

48
00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.870
♪ Take me again

49
00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.990
♪ And heaven. who knows

50
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.430
♪ Just where it will end!

51
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.350
♪ So dance. yeah. let's dance

52
00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.790
♪ Come on and dance... ♪

53
00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.240
MUSIC FADES TO ECHO

54
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.070
Feel no guilt. Inspector.

55
00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.270
I'm not talking to you.

56
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.270
Guilt has quick ears to an accusation.

57
00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.790
I'm not talking to you today!

58
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.470
I have always thought a
country should be judged

59
00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.560
on how it treats its insane.
rather than its sane.

60
00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.520
The stranger on our shores.
rather than those already home.

61
00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.630
Just do it.

62
00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.620
Just let go. River.

63
00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.320
TRAIN BRAKES SCREECH

64
00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.710
TV: 'The 26-year-old man has now
been named as Christopher Riley.

65
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.430
'Officers investigating the
drive-by shooting in October

66
00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.910
'of Detective Sergeant
Jacqueline Stevenson

67
00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.190
'believe Riley may have had key
information relating to the incident.

68
00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.630
'Girlfriend Tia Edwards

69
00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.150
'spoke to our Local Affairs
Correspondent. Alexis Wilby.

70
00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.350
'With only weeks to go until
the birth of her baby.

71
00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.950
'the death of Christopher Riley

72
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.030
'has caused my client
considerable distress.

73
00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.470
'Fundamental questions need to be asked.

74
00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.070
'Why is this officer still working.

75
00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.270
'when this young woman's
boyfriend has died?

76
00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.670
'My client had a bright
future ahead of her.

77
00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.830
'She'd just enrolled
on a course for nursing.

78
00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.310
'she was looking forward
to the birth of her baby.

79
00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.960
'Now. that future is shattered.'

80
00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.360
You know. you don't need
to carry all those files.

81
00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.080
They're all digitised. now.

82
00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:26.400
Only. it'll take you twice as long.

83
00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.270
You talk too much.

84
00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.320
If I don't talk. then
we have nothing but air.

85
00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.630
'We talk. She crosses the road.

86
00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.550
'she stops halfway.

87
00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.230
'She turns her head.

88
00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.880
'There's a look of recognition.'

89
00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.910
If Riley was driving that
car. maybe she knew him.

90
00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.030
- "If"?
- Did we ever arrest him?

91
00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.790
River. we found Stevie's DNA...

92
00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:27.960
- Maybe there was a grudge?
- .. inside the car.

93
00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.710
- Inside?
- Hmm.

94
00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.350
It nails Riley to this.
You're off the hook.

95
00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.760
Too right. there was a look of
recognition. She'd been in that car.

96
00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.230
They're asking the questions
we should be asking --

97
00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.110
what was a respected officer doing.

98
00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.710
- fraternising with a known drug dealer?
- No. Don't do that.

99
00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:52.430
Was there anything.
anything different about her?

100
00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.350
You worked with her that day. You
went for dinner. for Christ's sake.

101
00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:59.790
- You must have talked about something.
- We talked about nothing.

102
00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.070
We worked -- and then we had lunch.

103
00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:05.110
and then. we worked some
more. We went for a Chinese.

104
00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.430
She was not fraternising
with a drug dealer.

105
00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.910
Then what was she doing in that car?

106
00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.110
You can't deny where she comes from.

107
00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:14.830
Her family are alibied.

108
00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.110
but they used to run half of east London.

109
00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.710
She sent her own brother
down. A betrayal like that?

110
00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:22.560
That family never came back from it.

111
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.710
Tonight. at the wake. if you see anything.

112
00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.430
if you get a sense of anything...

113
00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.900
River. please?

114
00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.630
Marcus is waiting on your psych's report.

115
00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.270
so please. even if you don't think
it. even if you don't feel it.

116
00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:49.440
just try. please. try to
act like a normal person...

117
00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:53.480
CHRISSIE'S VOICE FADES TO ECHOES

118
00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:02.580
RIVER PANTS FOR BREATH

119
00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.680
Breathe.

120
00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:07.460
In and out.

121
00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.780
In and out.

122
00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:14.270
We've been here before.

123
00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.270
You just pretend.

124
00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.260
DNA inside the car?

125
00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.390
Anything else you didn't tell me?

126
00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.680
Your collar's not straight.

127
00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.910
We worked. We had lunch.
we worked some more.

128
00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.960
we went for Chinese.

129
00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.880
- We talked about nothing? Really?
- I don't remember.

130
00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.430
Loss of memory is a
sign of mental decline.

131
00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.350
- I don't remember.
- If you put 30 things on a tray.

132
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.800
a person would only
remember. on average. nine.

133
00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.500
That's ridiculous.

134
00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.880
Close your eyes.

135
00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:08.830
Soap. towels. hair in third sink.

136
00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.870
cracked ceiling. mirror. chipped.

137
00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:14.830
Fire extinguisher. broken cubicle door.

138
00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:19.470
fan. bin. chewing gum on sink.

139
00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:21.720
Ten. I got ten!

140
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.280
You've burnt your shirt.

141
00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:33.110
I've got a spare one hanging
up in my locker. if...

142
00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:35.150
It won't fit.

143
00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.540
Right.

144
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.070
Go back through the CCTV
footage from the Riley case.

145
00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.660
Look for anything they missed.

146
00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.840
Thank you.

147
00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.320
John?

148
00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.000
Sir.

149
00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:06.350
The coroner has already ruled
accidental death on Riley.

150
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.470
You got away with it.

151
00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.590
There are procedures put in place

152
00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:13.550
to protect police officers
from wrongful dismissal.

153
00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:16.870
So. it may take me time.

154
00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.920
but this isn't the place for you. River.

155
00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:25.880
I expect your psychiatric
report to support me in this.

156
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.430
Watch yourself. Riley's girlfriend's
been removed from the front desk.

157
00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.220
She was demanding to speak to you.

158
00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.470
Where are my flowers?

159
00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:54.150
For a skunk dealer?

160
00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.270
I was still a person.

161
00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:03.270
In Colorado. I'd be
considered a pharmacist.

162
00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:07.870
In Colorado. you can own an AK-47 and
graze your llama on public property.

163
00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.660
Hey. yo! Who you talking to. bruv?

164
00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.420
You're a nutter. you know?

165
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.800
Bleedin' nutter!

166
00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:46.360
MUSIC: Fisherman's Blues by The Waterboys

167
00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:27.440
Pigs.

168
00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.590
Stuck-up bitch. Who does she think she is?

169
00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:35.510
There seems to be an amnesty on
smoking. At least the beer's free.

170
00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.950
He's boring me shitless.

171
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.100
Oh. thank you. No more for you. then. eh?

172
00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.980
Your money's no good here.

173
00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:45.590
Hello. Jimmy.

174
00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.630
So. you got him?

175
00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:53.150
What was he -- some smacked-out
kid. looking to have a pop at a cop?

176
00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.800
Why did it have to be my sister?

177
00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:01.030
There was a time I could have
put a gun to somebody's head

178
00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.150
and found him myself.

179
00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:06.440
Now. I'm a reformed man.

180
00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:09.470
You've been gone a long time.

181
00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.920
Old sins cast long shadows.

182
00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:15.950
Everyone deserves a second chance.

183
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.400
I decapitated a man. River.

184
00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:21.060
I know.

185
00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:28.080
Watch your back tonight.

186
00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.630
MUSIC: Since You've Been Gone by Rainbow

187
00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.750
MICROPHONE FEEDS BACK

188
00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:39.920
All right. darling. All right. darling.

189
00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:44.920
I'm singing your song. sweetheart.

190
00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:53.390
♪ Since you been gone Since you been gone

191
00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:56.240
♪ I'm out of my head. can't take it

192
00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:01.230
♪ Could I be wrong? But
since you've been gone

193
00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:03.950
♪ You cast the spell. so break it

194
00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:08.190
♪ If you will come back

195
00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.340
♪ Baby. you know You'll
never do wrong... ♪

196
00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.960
MUSIC AND NOISE OF PUB FADES

197
00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.390
I'm embarrassed.

198
00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:26.160
She's a cow when she's sober and
Nelly Furtado when she's drunk!

199
00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:33.220
They don't even know what song I sang.

200
00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.920
Is it any wonder I left?

201
00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:39.710
And in the morning. they'll bury me --

202
00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:41.790
and the one person who'll be missing.

203
00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:44.190
the one person who should be there...

204
00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.980
I'm not family.

205
00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.510
Who says?

206
00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.470
Who says?

207
00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:54.830
Murderer! Murderer!

208
00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:58.070
Murderer! He didn't do
it. he didn't do it!

209
00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:00.320
Look at me. Look at me!

210
00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.870
Murderer! You killed him!

211
00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:06.830
- Mammy! - This time.
it was going to be OK!

212
00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.030
- You killed him!
- Oi!

213
00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:15.120
- Get off me! He didn't do it!
- All right. All right. love.

214
00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:19.030
It's all all right. Go on.

215
00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.420
Oh. get yourselves inside!

216
00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:23.860
Go on. inside.

217
00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:27.110
There. there. love...

218
00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:29.340
There. there...

219
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:32.670
When's that baby due. huh?

220
00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:35.190
You look about ready to drop.

221
00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:38.350
I hope they take it away from you.

222
00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.310
Is it that murdering.
druggie. smackhead scum's?

223
00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:42.590
- No!
- It's empty.

224
00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:45.270
You leave my buggy! You leave my buggy!

225
00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:49.030
It's all right. it's all right.
it's fine. There's no baby.

226
00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.350
- Just leave it alone!
- TIA SOBS

227
00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:54.710
It's all right. There. there...

228
00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.630
Leave it alone...

229
00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:01.670
She wants to talk to me.

230
00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.070
- She assaulted you.
- She knows something.

231
00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.510
She's a rambling mess. We've
interviewed her before.

232
00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.950
You can't get any sense out of her.

233
00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:11.270
- She just keeps saying the same thing. "He
didn't do it." - Well. maybe he didn't.

234
00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:14.150
She was sectioned ten months
ago. for drug-induced psychosis.

235
00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:17.270
- That's what happens when you smoke
too much skunk. - Let me try. at least.

236
00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.070
We're ringing around. trying to
find a unit that can take her in.

237
00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.110
It's the safest place for her.

238
00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.910
Her and Riley's first child
was taken away from them.

239
00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:28.270
Yes. and now she's pushing around
an empty buggy. for Christ's sake.

240
00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:32.390
Exactly. Come on. She's
got nothing. that kid.

241
00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:35.710
Just give me my buggy! I need it. please!

242
00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:37.750
Let her have the buggy!

243
00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.950
Tia...

244
00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.200
You can take the buggy.

245
00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:50.430
If I think that she's a danger
to herself. or to you...

246
00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.190
Rosa sits in with you. She's
the appropriate adult.

247
00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:56.940
If she thinks Tia can't
handle it. she will call it.

248
00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.950
You're going to take this one.

249
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.870
You are. You are. You are.

250
00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:05.910
I don't have that power.

251
00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:08.360
No. you all have the power.

252
00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:12.190
- All of you!
- Tia?

253
00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:14.590
- Sit down.
- No. just give me a chance.

254
00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:18.430
You only give up your power when
you don't think you have any.

255
00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:20.030
I'll be a good mum.

256
00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.020
You can show them.

257
00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:27.440
You can show them that you
can be better than this. Tia.

258
00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:31.400
Tia?

259
00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:54.910
Side effects hitting you hard today?

260
00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.500
What are you on -- Risperidone?

261
00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.710
Should take care of that.
if you take them every day.

262
00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:03.590
- No. I stopped taking them.
- That won't help. Tia.

263
00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.550
No. I looked it up. It's bad for the baby.

264
00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.950
If you take your medication
and get well. you're showing

265
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.510
that you can be responsible
for yourself and for a child.

266
00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:13.430
If you don't. you won't
see the world straight.

267
00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:15.880
Well. that can be overrated!

268
00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:21.140
Right. Tia?

269
00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.350
But if you don't. they will think

270
00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.880
that you're more of a threat to
the baby than you actually are.

271
00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.660
And you will love that baby...

272
00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.630
.. won't you?

273
00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:44.260
They said it was a good
size. on my last scan.

274
00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:49.480
- Then it's a boy.
- Everyone says that shit.

275
00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.460
Two to one. I'm right.

276
00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.560
You went for that scan the same
night my colleague was killed.

277
00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.580
And Riley wasn't with you.

278
00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:07.070
Where was he?

279
00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.910
If he didn't do it. who did?

280
00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:12.160
Who was driving the car?

281
00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.910
Tia. who drove the car that night?

282
00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.270
You're a queen when you're pregnant.

283
00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.510
And then. you're nothing. You're nothing.

284
00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.310
LIGHT BUZZES

285
00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:25.470
They're going to take this one away. too.

286
00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:27.260
Turn them off.

287
00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:32.000
- Turn off the light.
- You're going to take this one away.

288
00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.590
What the hell is going on?

289
00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:39.430
She's in no state to be interviewed.

290
00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:43.150
- Marcus...
- He's in no state to question her!

291
00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:46.070
- How long did you live with Riley?
- A long time.

292
00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:48.510
He looked after us. he took care of us.

293
00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:50.510
- But he wouldn't help
with the baby. - Us?

294
00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.470
We were going to do it right this time.

295
00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:56.710
He got me the car. and a cot.
A nice cot. He bought stuff.

296
00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:59.280
Who did? Who got you the car?

297
00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:04.400
- You're not talking about Riley now?
- Riley didn't care about the baby.

298
00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:07.550
He cared about drugs.

299
00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:09.830
I had to dope her up. it levelled her out.

300
00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:12.190
You try living with that kind of crazy.

301
00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:13.840
You nut-nut.

302
00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:18.230
River?

303
00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:19.680
River...

304
00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:23.430
- I want this interview stopped.
- Marcus. this is my case.

305
00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:26.280
Then handle it better than you are.

306
00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:31.870
I want to help you. Tia.
You're clean now. that's good.

307
00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:35.190
But I need you to tell me
who you're talking about.

308
00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:37.830
You have to talk to me.
You have to trust me.

309
00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:41.110
We can do it right this
time. We got a buggy...

310
00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:42.550
and we got baby wipes --

311
00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:45.070
- and we're going to look after
our baby. Me and... - Who?

312
00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:47.590
Me and... We're going to do it right.

313
00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:50.830
Tia. who? Who's "we"?

314
00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:52.150
DOOR OPENS

315
00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:56.670
No! No. no. they're going
to take it away from me. no!

316
00:22:56.720 --> 00:22:58.950
No! Please tell them I
can do it this time!

317
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:00.590
I can be a good mum!

318
00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:02.830
You've got to tell them
I can do it this time!

319
00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:05.910
Please! Don't let them
take it away from me!

320
00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:10.120
It's different now! You promised!
You promised to help me!

321
00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:17.590
She closed down. You won't get anything.

322
00:23:17.640 --> 00:23:19.750
You switched the light off.

323
00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:23.350
The buzzing -- the buzzing gets in
your head. How can anyone think?

324
00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:24.870
I...

325
00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:27.870
I have concerns that Riley's death
is affecting her mental stability.

326
00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:30.550
- She's... - She wasn't
talking about Riley. - No! No!

327
00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:34.470
Please. I don't want to. please...
No. No! Just get off me!

328
00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:36.630
Just get off me! No!

329
00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:39.270
Please. let me go. please... No!

330
00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:40.480
No!

331
00:23:57.760 --> 00:23:59.550
So. who was she talking about. then?

332
00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:01.670
Someone who cares for her.

333
00:24:01.720 --> 00:24:03.430
Someone who's helping her.

334
00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:06.870
If I'd only had a longer time with her...

335
00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:09.670
You always were good
with the window lickers.

336
00:24:09.720 --> 00:24:12.030
It's nice to see you found your tribe.

337
00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:14.550
- RIVER GRUNTS
- Admit it...

338
00:24:16.080 --> 00:24:17.820
.. you miss me.

339
00:24:21.320 --> 00:24:22.790
CAN DROPS

340
00:24:23.880 --> 00:24:26.550
If that's a Dr Pepper. it's mine.

341
00:24:28.640 --> 00:24:31.310
Must have got stuck halfway down.

342
00:24:43.760 --> 00:24:45.830
It swallowed my quid.

343
00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:48.200
Ta.

344
00:24:52.120 --> 00:24:54.510
There are no images of Riley in the car

345
00:24:54.560 --> 00:24:57.500
until the day after Stevie was killed.

346
00:25:01.480 --> 00:25:03.270
Before that. he's always on foot.

347
00:25:03.320 --> 00:25:07.430
Sprawl of kids around him --
running for him. it looks like.

348
00:25:07.480 --> 00:25:10.800
He's not got that car any
time before Stevie died.

349
00:25:12.240 --> 00:25:14.510
So. who had it?

350
00:25:14.560 --> 00:25:18.110
Then. I noticed some date discrepancies.

351
00:25:18.160 --> 00:25:21.160
Some login details that didn't look right.

352
00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:24.560
October 21st. 21.03.

353
00:25:26.640 --> 00:25:29.200
October 21st. 21.03.

354
00:25:33.240 --> 00:25:35.440
He was two miles away...

355
00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:39.230
.. and he certainly
wasn't driving that car.

356
00:25:39.280 --> 00:25:42.790
- When Stevie was shot...
- Riley was on the other side of town.

357
00:25:42.840 --> 00:25:44.580
CAN HISSES OPEN

358
00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:47.560
Finally.

359
00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:54.880
I might be a skunk dealer.
but I'm no murderer.

360
00:25:55.800 --> 00:25:58.200
I saved that for you. River.

361
00:25:59.120 --> 00:26:01.790
Got to find yourself another man.

362
00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:12.110
- You have to release it to the press.
- We went over everything...

363
00:26:12.160 --> 00:26:14.110
- You missed it.
- Yes. thanks for that. Einstein.

364
00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:16.430
You know. you've made this
twice as hard for yourself?

365
00:26:16.480 --> 00:26:18.870
- Do you know what the press
will do to you? - I was wrong.

366
00:26:18.920 --> 00:26:22.920
- They will crucify you!
- He was innocent. - Brilliant.

367
00:26:23.040 --> 00:26:26.350
- The boss has asked for Stevie's
accounts again. - For what?

368
00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:29.670
Weight Watchers subscriptions?
Payments for takeaways?

369
00:26:29.720 --> 00:26:31.630
.. And ten grand.

370
00:26:31.680 --> 00:26:34.350
withdrawn a week before she died.

371
00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:39.150
They're asking me if
she had a second phone.

372
00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:41.470
It's an obvious question.

373
00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:45.640
What am I going to do with this?

374
00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:49.480
Ira. could you just
give us a minute. please?

375
00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:02.560
If this kicks off...

376
00:27:02.920 --> 00:27:05.920
I don't know if I can do this any more.

377
00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:10.000
Grace is a hormonal mess...

378
00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:15.180
Nina's 12. and still wets the bed.

379
00:27:16.960 --> 00:27:19.790
Joe's idea of a gap year is not
getting up till 12 o'clock.

380
00:27:19.840 --> 00:27:21.440
and Peter...

381
00:27:23.160 --> 00:27:25.470
Don't have a fourth.

382
00:27:25.520 --> 00:27:28.680
A fourth is the last in. and
you never catch up with them.

383
00:27:33.680 --> 00:27:36.080
Go home. Clean yourself up.

384
00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:47.600
Mirtazepine.

385
00:27:49.200 --> 00:27:51.870
Someone else skipping their meds?

386
00:27:53.040 --> 00:27:55.430
For some. it's a little rum and coke.

387
00:27:55.480 --> 00:27:58.600
A little popper pill. a
little line. a bit of puff...

388
00:27:59.600 --> 00:28:02.200
Maybe you should try it. River.

389
00:28:02.600 --> 00:28:05.000
You do what you have to do.

390
00:28:14.360 --> 00:28:15.990
You read my file. man?

391
00:28:16.040 --> 00:28:19.190
I've been in care since I was three.
Robbing by the time I was ten.

392
00:28:19.240 --> 00:28:21.390
You think that girl Tia's any better?

393
00:28:21.440 --> 00:28:24.070
The baby will end up the same.

394
00:28:24.120 --> 00:28:26.150
All that crap doesn't end up in the sea.

395
00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:28.990
It washes back up the
shit pipe. back to here.

396
00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:31.390
But I was still worth something.

397
00:28:31.440 --> 00:28:34.440
I was still worth something to someone.

398
00:28:34.960 --> 00:28:37.360
Can you say the same thing?

399
00:28:48.560 --> 00:28:51.680
MUSIC: The Tide Is High by Blondie

400
00:28:54.800 --> 00:28:57.470
No-one ever called me Jacqueline.

401
00:28:58.480 --> 00:29:00.310
I hate carnations.

402
00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:05.270
♪ I'm not the kind of girl
who gives up just like that

403
00:29:05.320 --> 00:29:09.270
♪ Oh. no It's not the things you do... ♪

404
00:29:09.320 --> 00:29:13.310
Don't let her bully you.
and don't eat anything.

405
00:29:13.360 --> 00:29:16.100
It'll be out-of-date. frozen shit.

406
00:29:22.920 --> 00:29:25.390
- Hello. Frankie.
- All right?

407
00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:28.440
No-one got to bed till it had gone five.

408
00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:30.940
Will you hurry up?

409
00:29:34.600 --> 00:29:37.000
The service is at St Mark's.

410
00:29:37.800 --> 00:29:39.870
At the top.

411
00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:42.470
Father James died last
year. so it won't be him.

412
00:29:42.520 --> 00:29:45.640
But we've a very nice
gay who's taken over.

413
00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:48.270
What?

414
00:29:48.320 --> 00:29:50.070
You can't say that. Mum.

415
00:29:50.120 --> 00:29:52.190
Everyone knows he is.

416
00:29:52.240 --> 00:29:55.600
Would you get upstairs and
finish getting ready. Frankie?

417
00:30:01.080 --> 00:30:02.950
It's just family.

418
00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:06.630
Bridie...

419
00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:12.600
There'll be a story coming out
in the news today. about Riley.

420
00:30:15.320 --> 00:30:17.120
He didn't do it.

421
00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:19.870
No.

422
00:30:19.920 --> 00:30:21.430
No. no.

423
00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:24.680
We're releasing it to the
press. He was two miles away.

424
00:30:25.800 --> 00:30:27.270
It wasn't him.

425
00:30:27.320 --> 00:30:30.590
- Who. then?
- It's all right. Mammy.

426
00:30:30.640 --> 00:30:32.350
They can go back to watching us.

427
00:30:32.400 --> 00:30:34.600
Don't give me that crap.

428
00:30:35.280 --> 00:30:37.430
We were watching X Factor.

429
00:30:37.480 --> 00:30:40.420
We've told them that. again and again.

430
00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:45.390
My whole life you police
have taken. Every time.

431
00:30:45.440 --> 00:30:48.720
First. my son. Then. my husband...

432
00:30:50.240 --> 00:30:53.350
.. and then. you take my
daughter and put her in a uniform

433
00:30:53.400 --> 00:30:55.740
and you take her. as well.

434
00:30:57.080 --> 00:30:59.110
16 years...

435
00:30:59.160 --> 00:31:03.120
16 years. she didn't speak to her brother.

436
00:31:04.520 --> 00:31:06.270
Justice?

437
00:31:06.320 --> 00:31:10.320
The only real justice is when you
take the law into your own hands.

438
00:31:11.440 --> 00:31:13.640
I'll find who did this.

439
00:31:16.480 --> 00:31:18.220
Sure you will.

440
00:31:31.200 --> 00:31:33.470
Domestic violence arrest.

441
00:31:33.960 --> 00:31:35.790
Husband was drunk.

442
00:31:35.840 --> 00:31:38.440
Wife had called 12 times before.

443
00:31:39.400 --> 00:31:41.600
We made to arrest him...

444
00:31:42.240 --> 00:31:44.710
.. he slammed it in the door.

445
00:31:46.760 --> 00:31:49.190
I got you a pack of frozen peas.

446
00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:52.320
sat with you all night in
A&E. until they could see you.

447
00:31:53.880 --> 00:31:56.990
- It was only the tip.
- RIVER SNIGGERS

448
00:31:57.040 --> 00:32:00.800
And in the morning. we
ate Mars bars and...

449
00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:06.860
.. you told me stuff you'd
never told anyone before.

450
00:32:08.880 --> 00:32:10.420
DOOR OPENS

451
00:32:12.400 --> 00:32:14.390
I've been here for 15 minutes.

452
00:32:14.440 --> 00:32:17.540
I want you to knock 15
minutes off my time.

453
00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:25.340
I was a good nurse to you.

454
00:32:30.640 --> 00:32:33.040
Get some steak on that eye.

455
00:32:40.520 --> 00:32:41.920
River?

456
00:32:51.120 --> 00:32:53.350
Yesterday. with Tia...

457
00:32:53.400 --> 00:32:56.400
- you were very...
- It's my job. so...

458
00:32:57.080 --> 00:32:59.950
Even so. you were very good with her.

459
00:33:04.840 --> 00:33:06.840
She'll be all right.

460
00:33:07.320 --> 00:33:08.710
Sectioned?

461
00:33:08.760 --> 00:33:10.830
She needs medication.

462
00:33:11.200 --> 00:33:13.630
So. that's better for her. is it?

463
00:33:13.680 --> 00:33:16.220
Not always. For some people...

464
00:33:17.920 --> 00:33:19.270
.. I hope.

465
00:33:19.320 --> 00:33:22.470
So. it's better for the child
not to be with its mother?

466
00:33:22.520 --> 00:33:24.590
Farmed off somewhere?

467
00:33:27.840 --> 00:33:30.110
You lived with your
grandmother. didn't you?

468
00:33:30.160 --> 00:33:32.160
Yes. until I was 14.

469
00:33:32.800 --> 00:33:34.940
Where was your mother?

470
00:33:43.720 --> 00:33:45.920
What sort of day was it?

471
00:33:46.800 --> 00:33:48.550
Your last day with Stevie.

472
00:33:48.600 --> 00:33:51.030
They don't come in a
neat line. memories --

473
00:33:51.080 --> 00:33:54.120
they come in bits and
you have to try to...

474
00:33:55.480 --> 00:33:58.560
- .. Piece them together.
- Yeah. It was a...

475
00:34:00.240 --> 00:34:03.360
.. slow day. We'd been working
on a case for a long while.

476
00:34:05.640 --> 00:34:08.720
[RIVER SNORTS] I don't have
time for this. This is...

477
00:34:14.520 --> 00:34:15.760
I...

478
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:22.270
It was an ordinary day.

479
00:34:22.320 --> 00:34:24.590
We worked. we had lunch -- fast food.

480
00:34:24.640 --> 00:34:27.190
I tried a milkshake -- banana.

481
00:34:27.240 --> 00:34:30.310
And for some reason. she got it into
her head that she wanted Chinese.

482
00:34:30.360 --> 00:34:33.550
And I agreed to go with her to a
restaurant at the end of the day.

483
00:34:33.600 --> 00:34:35.230
What are you writing?

484
00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:36.870
Just notes for myself.

485
00:34:36.920 --> 00:34:40.020
So you can detangle. decipher and decide?

486
00:34:40.680 --> 00:34:41.880
Yes.

487
00:34:46.640 --> 00:34:48.790
So. it was a date. that night?

488
00:34:48.840 --> 00:34:51.670
- You'd gone on a date?
- With Stevie?

489
00:34:51.720 --> 00:34:52.920
Yes.

490
00:34:55.640 --> 00:34:57.840
These questions. it's...

491
00:34:58.440 --> 00:35:00.670
It's not natural to talk to someone.

492
00:35:00.720 --> 00:35:02.470
Yet talking to yourself is?

493
00:35:02.520 --> 00:35:04.860
I'm not talking to myself.

494
00:35:05.880 --> 00:35:09.120
There's always someone
there. Someone I'm talking to.

495
00:35:11.040 --> 00:35:16.310
"Note to self -- the patient comments
that he always talks to himself..."

496
00:35:16.360 --> 00:35:19.470
- Always? - But what is important
is that the patient can control it.

497
00:35:19.520 --> 00:35:22.750
he can distinguish between
what's there and what's not --

498
00:35:22.800 --> 00:35:27.000
- what is real and what's not.
- And can you? - Yes. I can.

499
00:35:29.080 --> 00:35:31.420
Have you done this before?

500
00:35:32.160 --> 00:35:35.260
Have you ever been prescribed medication?

501
00:35:36.160 --> 00:35:39.110
There's nothing -- nothing
on your medical records...

502
00:35:39.160 --> 00:35:42.350
On applying to the force. I submitted
to a full medical examination...

503
00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:44.070
- You know...
- .. which I passed...

504
00:35:44.120 --> 00:35:46.910
.. if you do not declare any
medical or psychiatric history...

505
00:35:46.960 --> 00:35:49.360
- .. successfully.
- River.

506
00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:54.400
Well. my BMI was a little high.

507
00:35:57.480 --> 00:36:00.580
You want me to do this report. don't you?

508
00:36:02.360 --> 00:36:04.670
If I don't do this
report. what will happen?

509
00:36:04.720 --> 00:36:07.590
- I'll lose my job.
- And then what?

510
00:36:08.360 --> 00:36:10.310
I'll drink a lot of whisky.

511
00:36:10.360 --> 00:36:12.100
And then what?

512
00:36:20.280 --> 00:36:22.950
Do you know Marcus McDonald well?

513
00:36:24.360 --> 00:36:25.960
Yes. you do.

514
00:36:26.800 --> 00:36:30.040
Well. since you were asking
me questions. I thought...

515
00:36:32.400 --> 00:36:33.790
In about two minutes.

516
00:36:33.840 --> 00:36:37.390
Dud. the very nice man from the
press office. will pass this door.

517
00:36:37.440 --> 00:36:41.470
In his hand. he will be holding an
official statement for the press.

518
00:36:41.520 --> 00:36:45.430
who are about to convene. also
just a few yards from here.

519
00:36:45.480 --> 00:36:49.230
They will learn that I... I
chased a man to his death.

520
00:36:49.280 --> 00:36:52.270
I chased an innocent man to his death --

521
00:36:52.320 --> 00:36:54.910
although the medical
coroner kindly has concluded

522
00:36:54.960 --> 00:36:57.230
that it was accidental...

523
00:36:58.160 --> 00:37:01.750
.. which is of very little
comfort to his girlfriend.

524
00:37:01.800 --> 00:37:04.670
His girlfriend. who's been sectioned.

525
00:37:05.320 --> 00:37:09.760
Although. who wouldn't. under
the circumstances. go mad?

526
00:37:13.200 --> 00:37:15.400
I'm just telling you...

527
00:37:15.920 --> 00:37:18.920
.. in case you'd like to note that down.

528
00:37:24.280 --> 00:37:26.230
They've found you out. I blame myself.

529
00:37:26.280 --> 00:37:29.270
- I'm not listening.
- I tried. but you have no small talk.

530
00:37:29.320 --> 00:37:31.390
It keeps people from asking questions.

531
00:37:31.440 --> 00:37:34.310
Weather. Football. "See anything
good on the TV last night?"

532
00:37:34.360 --> 00:37:35.700
Try it.

533
00:37:37.360 --> 00:37:39.760
You might surprise yourself.

534
00:37:43.680 --> 00:37:47.870
Ira -- CCTV pictures. Tracey
Estate. last 12 months.

535
00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:49.510
Riley got that car from somewhere.

536
00:37:49.560 --> 00:37:52.560
and Tia was talking about someone else.

537
00:38:09.320 --> 00:38:12.350
That kid. there...

538
00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:14.790
there. there...

539
00:38:14.840 --> 00:38:17.190
there. there. there...

540
00:38:17.240 --> 00:38:18.680
there.

541
00:38:20.080 --> 00:38:22.020
Always with a bike.

542
00:38:25.680 --> 00:38:27.550
Who is he?

543
00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:30.000
I need to talk to Tia again.

544
00:38:30.920 --> 00:38:33.270
Find out where they took her.

545
00:38:33.320 --> 00:38:35.590
I'll meet you downstairs.

546
00:38:58.000 --> 00:39:00.740
- Do you want the radio on?
- No.

547
00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:11.840
Have you ever been to China?

548
00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:18.110
You see. that's when you
could have asked a question.

549
00:39:18.160 --> 00:39:19.720
"No. Why?"

550
00:39:25.840 --> 00:39:28.430
I was up reading about it till three.

551
00:39:28.480 --> 00:39:30.480
Baby wouldn't sleep.

552
00:39:35.840 --> 00:39:37.580
Amazing place.

553
00:39:38.600 --> 00:39:41.000
Now. you say something else.

554
00:39:42.200 --> 00:39:44.110
Er...

555
00:39:44.160 --> 00:39:48.000
The fortune cookie was invented
in San Francisco in 1900.

556
00:39:54.640 --> 00:39:56.040
Serious?

557
00:40:00.120 --> 00:40:02.260
You can trust nothing.

558
00:40:20.480 --> 00:40:21.820
Hello.

559
00:40:25.160 --> 00:40:26.990
You were right. Tia.

560
00:40:27.040 --> 00:40:30.040
Riley couldn't have killed DS Stevenson.

561
00:40:33.160 --> 00:40:35.560
I need to find out who did.

562
00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:38.670
Did I do that?

563
00:40:38.720 --> 00:40:40.830
That?

564
00:40:40.880 --> 00:40:42.150
Yeah.

565
00:40:46.200 --> 00:40:48.400
They gave me something.

566
00:40:50.920 --> 00:40:53.190
At least it's quiet here.

567
00:40:55.200 --> 00:40:56.740
Yes. it is.

568
00:41:06.480 --> 00:41:08.630
Do you want anything. Tia?

569
00:41:08.680 --> 00:41:10.910
A cup of tea. or anything?

570
00:41:10.960 --> 00:41:12.240
No.

571
00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:15.040
You sure?

572
00:41:16.600 --> 00:41:19.070
I want to show you something.

573
00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:25.740
Is he the "we"?

574
00:41:28.920 --> 00:41:30.160
Tia?

575
00:41:33.520 --> 00:41:36.060
I didn't want to go on my own.

576
00:41:37.200 --> 00:41:39.030
You still worry...

577
00:41:39.080 --> 00:41:41.350
You still worry. when they...

578
00:41:41.400 --> 00:41:45.600
When they feel for the heartbeat.
you can't be sure. so...

579
00:41:46.400 --> 00:41:48.140
So. Bruno came.

580
00:41:49.440 --> 00:41:51.310
- Bruno?
- Yeah.

581
00:41:52.760 --> 00:41:56.550
He's different to the
others. He's a soft boy.

582
00:41:56.600 --> 00:41:58.550
He's kind.

583
00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:02.000
And he was with you at
the hospital that night.

584
00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:06.630
Is he the father?

585
00:42:08.520 --> 00:42:10.660
He'll make a good dad.

586
00:42:15.680 --> 00:42:17.880
I thought. this time...

587
00:42:18.280 --> 00:42:21.080
I thought. this time. with Bruno...

588
00:42:23.840 --> 00:42:26.440
He just wanted to get us a car.

589
00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:29.590
He didn't want me going on the bus.

590
00:42:29.640 --> 00:42:32.030
He didn't nick it until the next day.

591
00:42:32.080 --> 00:42:35.240
- The day after that copper got shot.
- So. he stole the car?

592
00:42:37.560 --> 00:42:40.760
Yeah. As soon as Riley
saw it. he wanted it.

593
00:42:41.360 --> 00:42:44.030
He didn't care that it was
hot. He didn't give a shit.

594
00:42:44.080 --> 00:42:46.350
There was nothing we could do.

595
00:42:46.400 --> 00:42:49.590
So. we need to talk to
Bruno. to tell him that...

596
00:42:49.640 --> 00:42:51.640
To tell him it's OK.

597
00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:55.880
We just need to know where
he got the car from.

598
00:42:56.200 --> 00:42:58.870
They're going to take the
baby away. for definite now.

599
00:42:58.920 --> 00:43:02.110
So. you need to show them that you're OK.

600
00:43:02.160 --> 00:43:04.830
You need to take your medication.

601
00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:08.240
You need to tell us where Bruno is.

602
00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:12.350
Maybe. with his help.
you can keep the baby.

603
00:43:12.400 --> 00:43:15.560
Maybe he can be the good
dad. until you're well again.

604
00:43:19.440 --> 00:43:21.950
You're all right. Tia.

605
00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:24.950
Even as you are. you're all right.

606
00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:27.670
Not everyone fits. in this world.

607
00:43:29.280 --> 00:43:31.020
Do you hear me?

608
00:43:36.440 --> 00:43:38.180
We can do this.

609
00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:40.800
We're all right.

610
00:43:41.880 --> 00:43:43.820
We just have to...

611
00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:46.980
.. Pretend?

612
00:43:49.240 --> 00:43:50.510
Yeah.

613
00:43:55.720 --> 00:43:57.680
Oh. is it now?

614
00:43:58.720 --> 00:44:01.710
Bruno. I need Bruno.

615
00:44:01.760 --> 00:44:04.560
We can get him. Tell us where he is.

616
00:44:07.840 --> 00:44:10.350
That's him.

617
00:44:10.400 --> 00:44:13.040
Bruno! Bruno. stop! It's OK!

618
00:44:17.680 --> 00:44:20.350
Slow down! You don't need to run!

619
00:44:32.640 --> 00:44:34.310
Bruno...

620
00:44:34.360 --> 00:44:36.510
BRUNO PANTS FOR BREATH

621
00:44:36.560 --> 00:44:39.500
We know you stole the car. Where from?

622
00:44:43.320 --> 00:44:45.350
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

623
00:44:45.400 --> 00:44:47.790
We know everything. Bruno.

624
00:44:47.840 --> 00:44:49.670
We talked to Tia.

625
00:44:49.720 --> 00:44:51.590
Is she all right?

626
00:44:52.600 --> 00:44:54.470
Is she all right?

627
00:44:55.960 --> 00:44:58.190
Is it coming?

628
00:44:58.240 --> 00:44:59.470
Yeah.

629
00:44:59.520 --> 00:45:01.310
Is it coming now?

630
00:45:01.360 --> 00:45:04.760
You have to tell me who
you stole the car from.

631
00:45:10.080 --> 00:45:12.110
So. it was dumped here?

632
00:45:12.160 --> 00:45:15.860
People do it all the time.
if it's a piece of shit.

633
00:45:16.920 --> 00:45:19.710
I came in early. Someone
was dropping it off.

634
00:45:19.760 --> 00:45:23.000
- Who? - I couldn't see.
It's dark in the winter.

635
00:45:24.400 --> 00:45:28.190
He was wearing this old coat.
Just dumped it at the gates.

636
00:45:28.240 --> 00:45:31.470
I called to him. but he kept walking.

637
00:45:31.520 --> 00:45:33.260
So. I took it.

638
00:45:39.400 --> 00:45:42.600
- She'll need her bag.
- We can get her bag.

639
00:45:42.920 --> 00:45:45.460
It's all back at Riley's flat.

640
00:45:45.760 --> 00:45:49.160
She needs her stuff --
nappies and shit. Please?

641
00:45:50.040 --> 00:45:51.280
OK.

642
00:46:08.720 --> 00:46:10.590
It's all in here.

643
00:46:14.640 --> 00:46:16.870
She's better off with him than me.

644
00:46:16.920 --> 00:46:19.120
Even if he's just a kid.

645
00:46:25.360 --> 00:46:27.960
I only went out for a milkshake.

646
00:46:29.040 --> 00:46:30.710
I'm so sorry.

647
00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:51.150
What do we tell Chrissie?

648
00:46:51.200 --> 00:46:54.000
We traced the car to the scrapyard.

649
00:46:55.080 --> 00:46:57.020
Anonymous tip-off.

650
00:46:58.080 --> 00:47:01.310
We need to get an ID on the
man who dropped off the car.

651
00:47:01.360 --> 00:47:03.590
We'll talk to Bruno in the morning.

652
00:47:03.640 --> 00:47:05.980
Let's give them the night.

653
00:47:08.960 --> 00:47:11.700
Do you think they'll be all right?

654
00:47:13.840 --> 00:47:15.380
I hope so.

655
00:47:19.920 --> 00:47:23.620
I don't know what I'd do
if my baby was taken away.

656
00:47:26.960 --> 00:47:29.760
You rush people. Don't rush people.

657
00:47:31.760 --> 00:47:33.120
Right.

658
00:47:36.080 --> 00:47:37.420
Right.

659
00:47:39.880 --> 00:47:41.630
What am I doing here?

660
00:47:41.680 --> 00:47:43.150
You were assigned.

661
00:47:43.200 --> 00:47:47.670
I've got a masters in IT. six years'
experience in violent crime...

662
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:50.390
I don't know what I'm doing here.

663
00:47:55.240 --> 00:47:58.180
And I'm going to be late for the quiz.

664
00:47:59.720 --> 00:48:02.680
Tonight? Terry mentioned it.

665
00:48:04.640 --> 00:48:06.310
In logistics?

666
00:48:10.200 --> 00:48:12.340
Do you talk to anyone?

667
00:48:12.920 --> 00:48:14.990
Not if I can help it.

668
00:48:16.560 --> 00:48:18.550
And you should clean your car.

669
00:48:18.600 --> 00:48:21.350
If you cleaned your car. it
might make you feel better.

670
00:48:21.400 --> 00:48:23.270
There's people who do that for you. now.

671
00:48:23.320 --> 00:48:25.590
You pay them. and they put
this stuff on your tyres.

672
00:48:25.640 --> 00:48:28.830
Makes your tyres look
new. A bit greasy. but new.

673
00:48:28.880 --> 00:48:30.510
- Stevie always...
- Yes.

674
00:48:30.560 --> 00:48:33.760
When it got bad. she'd
always tell me. so...

675
00:48:36.600 --> 00:48:38.800
So. I'm doing the same.

676
00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:49.000
I had an aunt who used to talk to herself.

677
00:48:54.120 --> 00:48:55.990
Did you like her?

678
00:48:58.720 --> 00:49:00.950
She tried to strangle my Uncle Ralph.

679
00:49:01.000 --> 00:49:02.600
RIVER LAUGHS

680
00:49:10.120 --> 00:49:12.260
What time is the quiz?

681
00:49:12.680 --> 00:49:14.020
Eight.

682
00:49:17.000 --> 00:49:20.500
- You don't want to be late.
- CAR ENGINE STARTS

683
00:49:57.520 --> 00:49:59.320
Close your eyes.

684
00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:02.620
I'm trying to work.

685
00:50:03.440 --> 00:50:05.350
Close your eyes.

686
00:50:05.400 --> 00:50:06.940
RIVER SIGHS

687
00:50:07.960 --> 00:50:10.100
What can you remember?

688
00:50:10.840 --> 00:50:12.520
Your eyes...

689
00:50:14.280 --> 00:50:16.150
.. blue-greenish.

690
00:50:16.680 --> 00:50:18.420
Nose. longish.

691
00:50:20.280 --> 00:50:22.070
Hair. brown.

692
00:50:22.120 --> 00:50:24.320
Blonde bits. sometimes.

693
00:50:25.680 --> 00:50:27.550
I don't remember.

694
00:50:29.520 --> 00:50:31.200
Teeth.

695
00:50:32.280 --> 00:50:34.020
Too many teeth.

696
00:50:34.920 --> 00:50:36.660
Top lip. thin.

697
00:50:38.760 --> 00:50:40.960
You're useless at this.

698
00:50:41.920 --> 00:50:45.400
Your cheeks explode when you laugh...

699
00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:51.670
You need to tell them what
we talked about that night.

700
00:50:51.720 --> 00:50:53.630
I don't remember.

701
00:50:53.680 --> 00:50:54.960
Liar.

702
00:50:58.840 --> 00:51:01.070
If this is your way of
helping with my passing...

703
00:51:01.120 --> 00:51:03.270
What passing? You're still here!

704
00:51:03.320 --> 00:51:06.060
- DOOR OPENS
- You're still here!

705
00:51:07.440 --> 00:51:08.840
River?

706
00:51:12.880 --> 00:51:14.750
Your questions...

707
00:51:18.880 --> 00:51:21.620
Yes. I've taken medication before.

708
00:51:23.040 --> 00:51:25.580
No. I've never disclosed this.

709
00:51:26.840 --> 00:51:29.870
Yes. Stevie helped me
control my condition.

710
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:32.920
No. I've never been formally diagnosed.

711
00:51:34.880 --> 00:51:39.720
Yes. I'm aware this is a
breach of police protocol.

712
00:51:44.080 --> 00:51:47.480
And when was the last
time I spoke to a friend?

713
00:51:49.160 --> 00:51:51.030
I don't have any.

714
00:51:53.760 --> 00:51:55.900
The only one I have...

715
00:51:57.880 --> 00:51:59.950
.. HAD is dead. so...

716
00:52:03.280 --> 00:52:05.020
FAINT LAUGHTER

717
00:52:09.280 --> 00:52:10.790
I'm a...

718
00:52:10.840 --> 00:52:12.550
I'm a good officer.

719
00:52:12.600 --> 00:52:14.430
But in this world. that's not enough.

720
00:52:14.480 --> 00:52:17.480
In this world. you have to be able to...

721
00:52:17.800 --> 00:52:21.520
.. nod and smile and drink a
pint and say. "How was your day?"

722
00:52:23.880 --> 00:52:26.480
In this world. no-one can be...

723
00:52:27.400 --> 00:52:30.340
.. different or strange. or damaged...

724
00:52:34.160 --> 00:52:36.360
.. or they lock you up.

725
00:52:39.920 --> 00:52:41.790
So. what do I do?

726
00:52:46.880 --> 00:52:48.750
What do I do now?

727
00:52:52.080 --> 00:52:53.950
You keep talking.

728
00:53:27.880 --> 00:53:29.960
CAR ENGINE STARTS

729
00:53:56.440 --> 00:53:59.040
It needs charging. you doughnut.

730
00:54:03.920 --> 00:54:05.750
So?

731
00:54:05.800 --> 00:54:07.870
I had a second phone.

732
00:54:16.360 --> 00:54:19.400
MUSIC: I'm In The Mood
For Dancing by The Nolans

733
00:54:36.680 --> 00:54:38.080
Go on...

734
00:54:39.200 --> 00:54:40.740
.. try it.

735
00:54:42.800 --> 00:54:44.200
Pretend.

736
00:54:45.400 --> 00:54:48.230
You might surprise yourself.

737
00:54:48.280 --> 00:54:53.710
♪ I'm in the mood for dancing. romancing

738
00:54:53.760 --> 00:54:57.110
♪ You know I shan't ever stop tonight

739
00:54:57.160 --> 00:55:00.750
♪ I'm in the mood for chancing

740
00:55:00.800 --> 00:55:02.870
♪ I feel like dancing

741
00:55:02.920 --> 00:55:05.910
♪ Ooh. from head to my toes

742
00:55:05.960 --> 00:55:07.870
♪ Take me again

743
00:55:07.920 --> 00:55:10.030
♪ And heaven. who knows

744
00:55:10.080 --> 00:55:12.270
♪ Just where it will end!

745
00:55:12.320 --> 00:55:16.270
♪ So dance. yeah. let's dance

746
00:55:16.320 --> 00:55:18.840
♪ Come on and dance

747
00:55:21.640 --> 00:55:25.230
♪ Dance. yeah. let's dance

748
00:55:25.280 --> 00:55:27.120
♪ Come on and dance... ♪
